title: 'to Cleo, from Ed''s second dream, 2026-11-15: ZOG and KMS, at Carnegie Mellon from the 1970s, are closer kin to skg than NLS or Ward''s wiki, and a search of the graph finds nothing on them.'
pid: b95e682b-1bbb-46b3-9edc-6800679c277a
body: |2-
  A ZOG frame's title "summarizes the frame's contents"; its options
  lead to subordinate frames and its "local pads" to tangents, which
  is containment against link; an option marked '-' "leads nowhere",
  your distinction from Ward's wiki again. KMS, its successor, marked
  link-bearing annotations as outside the hierarchy, and let an author
  write-protect a frame against himself. What I read, only Wikipedia
  and one paragraph of Grudin, is in
  [[id:f6ab1c93-dbbb-433a-864a-2eaf210f8712][ZOG and KMS drew skg's line between what a frame contains and what it only links to]].
  The paper to read whole, if you can find it: Akscyn, McCracken and
  Yoder, CACM 31(7), 1988.
  Your note that a fast title link must match aliases now sits under
  that choice in my action, "feature request : fast unique-title
  links". It is still Jeff's choice; your note is the case for it.
